mmunication"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Teamwork"},{"type":"p","text":"├── Field Safety"},{"type":"p","text":"└── Documentation"},{"type":"h","text":"Target Profile by Graduation"},{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, the student should have:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Strong emergency-care fundamentals"},{"text":"Trauma-assessment knowledge"},{"text":"BLS/CPR competency"},{"text":"Triage fundamentals"},{"text":"Mass-casualty response knowledge"},{"text":"Ambulance/emergency-service exposure"},{"text":"Patient movement and evacuation skills"},{"text":"Disaster-preparedness knowledge"},{"text":"Emergency communication skills"},{"text":"Incident-command awareness"},{"text":"Emergency equipment-management skills"},{"text":"Infection-control competency"},{"text":"Basic GIS and emergency mapping"},{"text":"Excel and data-analysis skills"},{"text":"Disaster-technology awareness"},{"text":"Significant emergency/field training"},{"text":"At least one disaster-response simulation or technology project"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Best Overall Positioning"},{"type":"flow","items":["Emergency & Trauma Care Technology","Emergency Department + Ambulance Training","Disaster Response Assistant","Mass-Casualty / Humanitarian / Emergency Operations Specialization","Disaster Response Coordinator","Emergency Management Leadership"]},{"type":"note","label":"Database mapping note","text":"Emergency & Trauma Care Technology → Disaster Response Assistant is a reasonable entry-level mapping when the role is defined as field emergency and disaster-response support. For greater precision, the database can later branch this career into Emergency Medical Technician, Disaster Medical Response Assistant, Humanitarian Response Assistant, Disaster Logistics Coordinator, and Emergency Operations Assistant."}]}]}